            "section_id": "prior_campaign_memory",
            "text": "- [u-L0034-03] Along the way down river, they encountered an elderly fisherman, whose net was stuck.\n- [u-L0034-04] Without missing a beat Bonogo out of selflessness and hopes for a giant fish to eat, dove into the water to find the damned net didn't have a fish, stupid useless net.\n- [u-L0043-04] Where Ephanna hopped on Bubbles back and followed after the runaway boats.\n- [u-L0034-02] Pippa a bright and talkative Gnome obsessed with crafting and understanding beer, hitched up Bubbles the Float Goat to her wagon full of kegs and led the crew to a dock and barge on the river.\n- [u-L0034-05] With some trial and error and stradling of boats Stafl and Baergrom I think pulled the net to surface to see it looked to be the corner beams of a roof.\n- [meta-session-0003-locations] session locations location places place setting map stonebridge Stone Bridge town; flood and rescue set-piece. longmont campaign longmont campaign campaign 1 rivers_edge_pub Grishna's tavern during the storm. rivers edge pub rivers edge pub wizards_tower_brewing_company Bardic retelling beat ties back to the brewery crawl. wizards tower brewing company wizards tower brewing company mirathorn Festival-city hook named in closing beats; table-facing route placeholder.\n- [u-L0005-02] Finding a sack of gems, some mystery potions on corpses in the well, and perhaps most importantly bashing down a wall to reveal a room full of healing potions and alchemical tools and ingredients of and ancient and incredible design.\n- [u-L0007-01] Since this room was not part of the original contract, and really neither was the rest of this god forsaken place, they negotiated with Glowkindle for the right to stash gear in the hidden alchemy room.\n- [u-L0011-02] Will they had back to Stonebridge to say hi to Grishna at the River's Edge Pub?\n- [u-L0036-01] Once at StoneBridge and unloading beer, it became clear a storm was coming.\n- [u-L0043-02] Stafl and Caelynn cut loose a dinghy and let the river take them after Bonogo, with only a net with light cast on it and hope.\n- [u-L0043-03] Ephanna and the mage hand coaxed Bubbles to the lasso and were able to get her to the dock across the ice path and rushing river.\n- [u-L0045-01] Bonogo was rescued, the wet adventurers headed to the Pub to find a damp, but generally relieved, safe, and drying town.\n- [u-L0036-03] Inside was the evening crew, Grishna, patrons, and another bard!\n- [u-L0036-04] Who Stafl immediately joined in a jam with that undoubtedly demonstrated his superior song craft and bardic talents.\n- [u-L0040-11] Stafl began banging on doors and assisting townfolk escape the flood and gather at the pub on high ground.\n- [u-L0041-04] Thoroughly fermented) Bonogo dives into the river with full trust in Baergrom to hold the rope, which is immediately torn out of Baergrom's hand.\n- [u-L0011-03] Will they follow up on the errant thought of what if there is more to the Wizard's Tower?\n- [u-L0034-01] Ready for some rest, ready to not be covered in the sweat and ichor of the day, Caelynn, Karsemine, Stafl, Baergrom, and Ephanna accepted the offer of a ride to StoneBridge with Pippa.\n- [u-L0036-05] After some excellent drinks and music, Pippa realizes the loud drumming isn't just the bard, but a torrent of rain on the roof excuses herself to check on Bubbles.\n- [u-L0040-05] Rapidly searching around Bubbles is found wildly bleating on a rock in the river.\n- [u-L0041-05] Unprepared for the speed with which the river carries Bonogo away, the rope and Bonogo are gone.\n- [u-L0043-01] In the face of a rapidly deteriorating situation, Karsemine cast Zephyr strike and ran down the bank, shooting arrows at wear Bonogo probably was.\n- [u-L0004-01] Unseasonable torrential rains floods wherever the players are, non combat problem solving.\n- [u-L0004-02] They have to keep themselves alive, and save townsfolk.\n- [u-L0020-01] Ephanna uses mage hand to lasso Bubbles on the rock.\n- [u-L0030-01] Ephanna's mage hand succeeds the second time and lassos Bubbles, lead her to Ephanna.\n- [u-L0036-02] Hitching up Bubbles and the barge, into the River's Edge Pub for a welcome round of beers and some bragging to Grishna about their adventures.\n- [u-L0036-06] Gone for a few moments, during a pause in the retelling of the day's events, weeping is heard from another table, followed by a piercing yell in between cascades of rain off the roof.\n- [u-L0040-02] Gripping onto the front of the pub holding on in rushing water up to her waste.\n- [u-L0040-06] Out on a rickety dock, shaking in the flood and downpour, the river frothing, rapids crashing all around as it wildly rushed.\n- [u-L0040-08] Stafl runs for help, and gathers townfolk to set nets across the river.\n- [u-L0041-01] Sending the mage hand and rope out to Bubbles, the Float Goat panics and bites, destroying the mage hand and dropping the rope into the water.\n- [u-L0041-06] The only remenant, the end of the rope whipping across the top of the river, vanishing out of sight.\n- [meta-session-0001-locations] session locations location places place setting map stonebridge Starting town; no location hub in corpus yet. longmont campaign longmont campaign campaign 1 rivers_edge_pub Grishna's tavern in Stonebridge. rivers edge pub rivers edge pub wizards_tower_brewing_company Glowkindle's brewery and rat-clearing site. wizards tower brewing company wizards tower brewing company shatter_mages_tower Referenced as containing the magma spider threat. shatter mages shatter mages tower\n- [u-L0003-01] Adventure hook, hear about a mysterious artifact while celebrating.\n- [u-L0005-03] They unfortunately haven't the first clue how to use them, but they are cool!\n- [u-L0014-01] Stafl wrote and played an incredible song that woo'd the town in the retelling of the Wizard's Tower Brewery adventure.\n- [u-L0018-01] Players heard Pippa yelling and immediately ran out to help find Bubbles.\n- [u-L0040-07] a lasso was made and handed to a mage hand Ephanna created.\n- [u-L0040-09] Bonogo and Baergrom prepare for Bonogo to dive in.\n- [u-L0003-01] Adventure hook, hear about a mysterious artifact while celebrating.\n- [u-L0006-01] Big beats :\n- [u-L0007-01] Since this room was not part of the original contract, and really neither was the rest of this god forsaken place, they negotiated with Glowkindle for the right to stash gear in the hidden alchemy room.\n- [u-L0007-03] Bonogo, having very little awareness or care for the cost of things, and greatly enjoying the beer, bought a Firkin of ale for two gold.\n- [u-L0008-01] Rode with Pippa and fell in love with Bubbles.\n- [u-L0009-01] After making pretty good money, 25 gp each, a bit of loot, and learning a lot about the dangers of clearing rats out of basements, the group decided to stick together and see where the winds take them.",
